*>--- conformance-case
*> id: pb3829_random_fraction_rounded_store
*> rules: [GR-14.7.4.3-2, GR-14.7.4.3-3, GR-14.7.4.3-4, GR-14.7.4.3-5,
*>    GR-14.7.4.3-6, GR-14.7.4.3-8, GR-14.7.4.3-9, GR-14.7.4.3-10,
*>    GR-14.9.8.4-2, GR-14.7.5-3, RV-15.75.4-1, RV-15.75.4-2,
*>    RV-15.42.4-1]
*> accept: [2014]
*> source-format: free
*> portable: unverified
*>---
*> kb/Work PB3829 (the WiseOwl half of 14.7.4-ROUNDED/pb3829_rounded_bounded_function_modes): RANDOM and
*> FRACTION-PART of a FLOAT-LONG item return implementor-defined values (15.75.4 2) "For a given seed value on a
*> given implementation, the sequence of pseudo-random numbers will always be the same."; a FLOAT-LONG content is
*> the implementor's binary64), so the returned values are DISPLAYed first and every leg is derived from them:
*>    RANDOM(97090)            = 0.99999789288267393...   (the seeded generator's first draw, CONFORMANCE.md DOC-A.1-145)
*>    FRACTION-PART(5.9999999996 FLOAT-LONG) = 0.99999999959999996690... (the binary64 of 5.9999999996, minus 5)
*> 15.75.4 1) "The returned value is greater than or equal to zero and less than one." bounds the RETURNED value;
*> the stored one follows 14.9.8.4 2) (14.6.8, 14.7.4, 14.7.5): each leg is that value rounded per 14.7.4.3 at the
*> receiver's scale, so every nearest mode and AWAY-FROM-ZERO / TOWARD-GREATER give 1.0000 and 1.00 (R4, R2) and
*> a trailing-P receiver (RP, PIC S9P) gives 10 under the directed modes away from zero.
*> 14.7.5 3) "if, after radix point alignment and any applicable rounding specifications, the result of an
*> arithmetic statement is further from zero than permitted for the associated resultant data item" is a size
*> error: RANDOM(97090) ROUNDED into V4 (PIC SV9999, no integer position) is 1.0000, so ON SIZE ERROR runs and V4
*> keeps 0; without the phrase the store keeps the low-order digits (14.6.13.1.3, WiseOwl's documented
*> disposition), .0000; ROUNDED MODE TRUNCATION fits (.9999) and takes NOT ON SIZE ERROR.
*> WHY EACH LEG CAN FAIL: a store that cuts a rounded value back below 1 (the codomain clamp PB3829 removed) prints
*> 0.9999 / 0.99 / 00 on the rounding legs and takes NOT ON SIZE ERROR with .9999 in V4.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. PB3829RANDFRAC.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 R4 PIC S9V9999 SIGN LEADING SEPARATE.
01 R2 PIC S9V99 SIGN LEADING SEPARATE.
01 RP PIC S9P SIGN LEADING SEPARATE.
01 V4 PIC SV9999 SIGN LEADING SEPARATE.
01 X19 PIC 9V9(19).
01 FSRC USAGE FLOAT-LONG.
01 FNEG USAGE FLOAT-LONG.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
           MOVE 5.9999999996 TO FSRC
           MOVE -5.9999999996 TO FNEG
           COMPUTE X19 = FUNCTION RANDOM(97090)
           DISPLAY "RANDOM(97090)  " X19
           COMPUTE X19 = FUNCTION FRACTION-PART(FSRC)
           DISPLAY "FRACTION-PART  " X19
           COMPUTE R4 = FUNCTION RANDOM(97090)
           DISPLAY "R4 RANDM NONE " R4
           COMPUTE R4 ROUNDED = FUNCTION RANDOM(97090)
           DISPLAY "R4 RANDM RND  " R4
           COMPUTE R4 ROUNDED MODE AWAY-FROM-ZERO = FUNCTION RANDOM(97090)
           DISPLAY "R4 RANDM AFZ  " R4
           COMPUTE R4 ROUNDED MODE NEAREST-AWAY-FROM-ZERO = FUNCTION RANDOM(97090)
           DISPLAY "R4 RANDM NAFZ " R4
           COMPUTE R4 ROUNDED MODE NEAREST-EVEN = FUNCTION RANDOM(97090)
           DISPLAY "R4 RANDM NE   " R4
           COMPUTE R4 ROUNDED MODE NEAREST-TOWARD-ZERO = FUNCTION RANDOM(97090)
           DISPLAY "R4 RANDM NTZ  " R4
           COMPUTE R4 ROUNDED MODE TOWARD-GREATER = FUNCTION RANDOM(97090)
           DISPLAY "R4 RANDM TG   " R4
           COMPUTE R4 ROUNDED MODE TOWARD-LESSER = FUNCTION RANDOM(97090)
           DISPLAY "R4 RANDM TL   " R4
           COMPUTE R4 ROUNDED MODE TRUNCATION = FUNCTION RANDOM(97090)
           DISPLAY "R4 RANDM TRUN " R4
           COMPUTE R4 = FUNCTION FRACTION-PART(FSRC)
           DISPLAY "R4 FRACP NONE " R4
           COMPUTE R4 ROUNDED = FUNCTION FRACTION-PART(FSRC)
           DISPLAY "R4 FRACP RND  " R4
